  "report_period": "Week 2 (2nd Jan to 9th Jan 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "CMB.Tech have committed their Capesize \"Golden Magnum\" 179/2009 Daewoo, Korea (SS 11/2029, DD 05/2027, Scrubber fitted) to Chinese interests at USD 28,7 mill, while the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Europe\" 179/2010 Daewoo, Korea (SS 11/2030, DD 12/2028) from Orion Reederei was sold to Chinese interests also at USD 30,9 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Cape Providence\" 179/2009 Daewoo, Korea (SS 06/2029, DD 02/2026) was sold in early December at USD 28 mill. On the Handysize sector, Turkish owners committed the \"Fethiye-M\" 38/2011 Spp, Korea (SS/DD 09/2026) to Greek interests at USD 12,9 mill. Remind you that back in October, the two-years-younger sister vessel \"Dogan\" 38/2013 Spp, Korea (SS 10/2028, DD 01/2027) was sold at USD 14,8 mill.",
    "tankers": "Chandris Hellas have committed the VLCC \"Oceanis\" 320/2011 Samsung, Korea (SS/DD 04/2026, Scrubber fitted) to clients of Sinokor at USD 68,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Oceanic Fortune\" 320/2010 Hyundai, Korea (SS 01/2030, DD 04/2028, Scrubber fitted) was sold in late October at USD 57 mill. In addition, clients of Sinokor also acquired the \"Nissos Psara\" 301/2011 IHI, Japan (SS/DD 02/2026, Scrubber fitted) from Kyklades Maritime at USD 68 mill. Note that Kyklades Maritime purchased the vessel (ex name \"FPMC C Knight\") back in September at USD 55 mill. The LR1 \"Pelagic Tope\" 76/2008 Dalian, China (SS 03/2028, DD 03/2026) was committed at USD 14 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older \"Ryvingen Sun\" 74/2007 New Century, China (SS 05/2027, DD 08/2028) was sold back in October at USD 14,2 mill. Chios Navigation Hellas have committed the MR2 \"Doric Pioneer\" 51/2013 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 01/2028, DD 01/2026) at USD 29,5 mill, while the two-years-younger \"Nord Superior\" 49/2015 Stx, Korea (SS 01/2030, DD 04/2027, Scrubber fitted) of Norden was sold in December at USD 33,7 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low/mid usd 8,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/12,000 pd. A number of Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 8,000/11,000 pd range. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 8,000/10,000 pd. Indian trips via South America into China were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast- US Gulf into India or China were reported at the level of usd 18,000/20,000 pd. Inter-Continental trips via US Gulf were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 14,000/15,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K/500K. North Coast South American trips into West Africa were fixed around usd 12,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 400K.East Coast South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 15,000/16,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 500K/600K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 14,000 pd for 17/19 months employment basis delivery East Coast India. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 16,500 pd basis delivery China for 6/10 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 10,000/11,000 pd. number of Indonesian into China were fixed around usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into East Coast India were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. West African trips via South Africa into China were reported at the level of usd 11,000/13,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 25,000/27,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Japanese into Continent were reported at the level of usd 11,000/12,000 pd. Trips from North China into East Coast India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Indonesian and Australian trips into China were reported fixed in the usd 7,000/10,000 pd range. Arabian Gulf trips into South East Asia were fixed around usd 8,000/10,000 pd. West African trips into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 6,000/8,000 pd. Inter-Mediterranean trips were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. East Coast South American trips into West Coast South America were fixed around usd 20,000/22,000 pd. East Coast South American coastal trips were reported at the level of usd 17,000/19,000 pd. A small Handysize was fixed on a period at the usd 10,500 pd basis delivery South East Asia for 1 year employment."
    }
  },
